WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.804
Early the next morning, Katie ran up the hill to the pond.

2
00:00:06.805 --> 00:00:11.231
Dad and Joy were already working on the tree house steps.

3
00:00:11.232 --> 00:00:16.415
"Morning, Dad," called Katie, climbing into the back of the truck.

4
00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:21.757
She looked in the old bucket and pulled out the pulley. "What's this?"

5
00:00:21.758 --> 00:00:25.823
"It's a pulley of course," said Joy.

6
00:00:25.824 --> 00:00:28.830
"What's it for?" asked Katie.

7
00:00:28.831 --> 00:00:31.964
"You'll see," Joy answered.

8
00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:34.332
"Hey," said Katie.

9
00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:37.821
"I can use this pole for my wind sock."

10
00:00:37.822 --> 00:00:41.245
"What's a wind sock?" asked Joy.

11
00:00:41.246 --> 00:00:45.065
"You'll see," answered Katie.

12
00:00:45.066 --> 00:00:48.743
Pieces of the tin roof were spread on the grass.

13
00:00:48.744 --> 00:00:52.181
Dad opened a can of dark blue paint.

14
00:00:52.182 --> 00:00:54.724
"Here's a brush," he said to Joy.

15
00:00:54.725 --> 00:00:56.810
"Do you want to help, Katie?"

16
00:00:56.811 --> 00:01:01.298
"Nope," Katie said and jumped down from the truck.

17
00:01:01.299 --> 00:01:07.627
"Mom and I are working on something. See you later."

18
00:01:07.628 --> 00:01:18.319
Joy dipped her brush into the paint and carefully painted the first piece of tin.

19
00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:20.852
"This roof has to look perfect,"

20
00:01:20.853 --> 00:01:25.132
Joy said to herself as she turned to dip her brush again.

21
00:01:25.133 --> 00:01:30.597
When she turned back, Magoo was sitting on the freshly painted tin.

22
00:01:30.598 --> 00:01:35.063
"Magoo!" she said. "It's wet paint!"

23
00:01:35.064 --> 00:01:41.084
Magoo got up and licked Joy's face, his blue tail wagging happily.

24
00:01:41.085 --> 00:01:46.109
"Get out of here," cried Joy. "You'll spill the paint."

25
00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:49.560
Magoo leaped back and sat down again.

26
00:01:49.561 --> 00:01:52.703
"Good boy," said Joy.

27
00:01:52.704 --> 00:01:54.912
Magoo watched Joy paint.

28
00:01:54.913 --> 00:01:59.243
His eyes were fixed on the brush as it moved back and forth.

29
00:01:59.244 --> 00:02:03.723
Then he reached out and touched the brush with his paw.

30
00:02:03.724 --> 00:02:06.187
"Stop!" cried Joy.

31
00:02:06.188 --> 00:02:08.980
"Do you want to be a blue Magoo?"

32
00:02:08.981 --> 00:02:14.981
The dog pulled back his blue paw and gave Joy a sorry look.

33
00:02:14.982 --> 00:02:21.990
By noon the steps were finished, the tin pieces were painted, and Dad was building the walls.

34
00:02:21.991 --> 00:02:25.740
Joy and Magoo were lying in the grass.

35
00:02:25.741 --> 00:02:35.354
They were both covered with paint: her shirt, his paws, her knees, his tail, her chin, his ear.

36
00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:36.983
But Joy didn't care.

37
00:02:36.984 --> 00:02:40.315
The tree house would be finished soon!

38
00:02:40.316 --> 00:02:44.496
The next afternoon, Dad put in the door and the window.

39
00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:47.721
Finally he nailed down the roof.

40
00:02:47.722 --> 00:02:50.754
"It's done!" shouted Joy.

41
00:02:50.755 --> 00:02:54.953
Katie, Mom, and Grandpa ran from the house to see.

42
00:02:54.954 --> 00:02:58.872
Mom brought a flowerpot filled with daisies.

43
00:02:58.873 --> 00:03:00.659
"Put it in the bucket, Mom!"

44
00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:03.543
Joy shouted from the tree house.

45
00:03:03.544 --> 00:03:08.260
The bucket was sitting on the ground with a rope tied to its handle.

46
00:03:08.261 --> 00:03:13.120
The rope was attached to the pulley, which was attached to the roof.

47
00:03:13.121 --> 00:03:16.374
Mom set the flowers in the bucket.

48
00:03:16.375 --> 00:03:19.936
"Now watch this," called Joy.

49
00:03:19.937 --> 00:03:25.079
She pulled on the rope, the pulley turned, and the bucket rose.

50
00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:27.962
Joy lifted the daisies out of the bucket.

51
00:03:27.963 --> 00:03:30.125
"Come on up, Mom!"

52
00:03:30.126 --> 00:03:37.275
One by one everyone took a turn looking out on the Donovans' land from the tree house.

53
00:03:37.276 --> 00:03:41.218
Everyone opened and shut the tree house door.

54
00:03:41.219 --> 00:03:46.618
They looked out the window and tried out the pulley.

55
00:03:46.619 --> 00:03:52.396
"Let's give a big cheer for Dad and Joy!" shouted Katie.

56
00:03:52.397 --> 00:03:56.221
Mom, Grandpa, and Katie clapped and cheered.

57
00:03:56.222 --> 00:04:00.036
Dad bowed. Joy beamed.

58
00:04:00.037 --> 00:04:02.646
"One more thing," said Katie.

59
00:04:02.647 --> 00:04:06.680
"Dad put up the new wind sock on the tree house roof.

60
00:04:06.681 --> 00:04:10.584
Look! You can see it hanging from the pole."

61
00:04:10.585 --> 00:04:13.232
Everyone looked up at the wind sock.

62
00:04:13.233 --> 00:04:15.830
"Mom helped me make it."

63
00:04:15.831 --> 00:04:20.026
"Wow!" said Joy.

64
00:04:20.027 --> 00:04:25.688
"A wind sock tells us the strength and direction of the wind," explained Katie.

65
00:04:25.689 --> 00:04:30.179
"When the wind is still, the wind sock just hangs."

66
00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:34.079
"Like it's doing right now," said Grandpa.

67
00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:36.558
"That's right," Katie said.

68
00:04:36.559 --> 00:04:42.049
"But when the wind is strong, the wind sock flies straight out!"

69
00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:46.191
Katie paused and opened her eyes extra wide.

70
00:04:46.192 --> 00:04:50.659
"And if that wind is coming from the southwest, look out!

71
00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:53.814
It might be tornado time!"

72
00:04:53.815 --> 00:04:59.856
"That's pretty cool, Katie," said Joy. "Thanks!"

